<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5174bab391e2443a3fdda3515d14a344f343ffac" commit="01df844631cf510c2131f6fb8e338b1d216b3cc9" commit_message="[Chameleon] LCM standalone UI interface  LcmInterface is the main instance of standalone UI system, which brings up LCM display module, key controller, and LED controller, and uses the XMLRPC proxy of chameleond to call chameleon functions.  Moreover, the finite state machine of showing UI menu and information on LCM display is included. LcmInterface is also the consumer of event queue to process key events.  Right now only partial functions mentioned in design document are implemented. We are going to add them step by step to make standalone UI more powerful.  BUG=chromium:569733 TEST=manual test. Push code onto chameleon and test. chameleon&gt; cd /usr/lib/python2.7/site-packages/chameleond chameleon&gt; python  &gt;&gt;&gt; import xmlrpclib &gt;&gt;&gt; from chameleond.utils.lcm_interface import LcmInterface &gt;&gt;&gt; from chameleond.utils.lcm_queue import LcmEventQueue &gt;&gt;&gt; chameleond_proxy = xmlrpclib.ServerProxy('http://0.0.0.0:9992', allow_none=True) &gt;&gt;&gt; displayd = LcmInterface(chameleond_proxy, LcmEventQueue) &gt;&gt;&gt; displayd.Run() (You will see the boot screen shown on LCM display, press any key to start browsing menu and executing functions. H_KEY3:left H_KEY2:up H_KEY1:down H_KEY0:right)  Change-Id: I5174bab391e2443a3fdda3515d14a344f343ffac Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329356 Commit-Ready: Pin-chih Lin &lt;johnylin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Pin-chih Lin &lt;johnylin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329356" owner_email="johnylin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/chameleon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/chameleon" ref="refs/changes/56/329356/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I734df2058256c79b7bebc8ed324bbff04a605460" commit="af79398cf5f5d7ca6ffe2c64616875eb0b84647a" commit_message="Test to capture performance data from CFM device  This test enrolls ChromeOS device into hotrod mode and captures device usage data including cpu, memory and temperature data and uploads it to Google Cloud Storage as part of the test logs.  BUG=chromium:591257 TEST=Tested on local setup.  Change-Id: I734df2058256c79b7bebc8ed324bbff04a605460 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329965 Commit-Ready: harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rohit Makasana &lt;rohitbm@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329965" owner_email="harpreet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/65/329965/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="I7d0aec0b60afd8506a9136ed62fd647caec748aa" commit="45a49283655ef6008dc9b14f6f8465e3a49ec683" commit_message="CHROMIUM: CONFIG: Enable VGEM on exynos  In an effort to enable VGEM everywhere, I am flipping the switch on kernel 3.8 + exynos.  BUG=none TEST=untested  Change-Id: I7d0aec0b60afd8506a9136ed62fd647caec748aa Signed-off-by: Stphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/314891 Commit-Ready: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="314891" owner_email="marcheu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/